WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:00.138 --> 00:00:02.414
- 'Cause I was so worried
about being accepted.

00:00:02.414 --> 00:00:03.423
These people to accept me.

00:00:03.423 --> 00:00:04.787
These people to accept me.

00:00:04.787 --> 00:00:06.810
And when the don't, you die.

00:00:06.810 --> 00:00:08.555
I'm like a cultural anthropologist, man.

00:00:08.555 --> 00:00:10.888
I just love to just sit and soak up stuff.

00:00:10.888 --> 00:00:12.145
It's better to create something

00:00:12.145 --> 00:00:14.353
that other people criticize
than to create nothing

00:00:14.353 --> 00:00:16.030
and criticize others.

00:00:16.030 --> 00:00:16.873
- Hello Believe Nation.

00:00:16.873 --> 00:00:18.021
I'm Evan Carmichael.

00:00:18.021 --> 00:00:20.353
My one word is believe and I believe

00:00:20.353 --> 00:00:22.378
that entrepreneurs are going to solve all

00:00:22.378 --> 00:00:24.466
of the major problems of the world.

00:00:24.466 --> 00:00:25.622
So to help you on your journey,

00:00:25.622 --> 00:00:28.418
today we're going to learn
from hip-hop artist Lecrae

00:00:28.418 --> 00:00:31.282
and my take on his top
ten rules for success.

00:00:31.282 --> 00:00:33.336
Rule number six is my personal favorite

00:00:33.336 --> 00:00:35.911
and I'd love to know which
one you guys like the best.

00:00:35.911 --> 00:00:37.345
And as always guys, as you're watching

00:00:37.345 --> 00:00:39.417
if you hear something that
really resonates with you

00:00:39.417 --> 00:00:41.327
please leave it down
in the comments below,

00:00:41.327 --> 00:00:43.877
put quotes around it so
other people can be inspired

00:00:43.877 --> 00:00:46.365
and when you write it
down it's much more likely

00:00:46.365 --> 00:00:48.543
to stick for yourself as well.

00:00:48.543 --> 00:00:49.376
Enjoy.

00:00:53.219 --> 00:00:55.802
(upbeat music)

00:01:02.887 --> 00:01:04.832
- Just one thing I learned about success.

00:01:04.832 --> 00:01:06.579
Success, you know, stop comparing yourself

00:01:06.579 --> 00:01:08.374
to everybody else 'cause
that ain't going to make you.

00:01:08.374 --> 00:01:10.252
Success is not what
you do compared to them

00:01:10.252 --> 00:01:12.191
it's what you do compared to
what you do you was made to do.

00:01:12.191 --> 00:01:13.862
So you got to compete against yourself

00:01:13.862 --> 00:01:18.029
and push yourself to the limits
that you need to run toward.

00:01:19.098 --> 00:01:20.064
What was you made to do?

00:01:20.064 --> 00:01:22.584
Go do that and don't let
anybody dissuade you.

00:01:22.584 --> 00:01:24.298
Don't let anybody say
you can't do it, man.

00:01:24.298 --> 00:01:25.834
Just keep pushing, keep going.

00:01:25.834 --> 00:01:28.799
I would tell myself to brace
yourself for a real struggle,

00:01:28.799 --> 00:01:32.787
for real pain, for death,
for loss, for hurt.

00:01:32.787 --> 00:01:35.726
And then as an artist I would tell myself,

00:01:35.726 --> 00:01:38.282
you know, what I say and I put
on the back of the book, too.

00:01:38.282 --> 00:01:39.630
If you live for people's acceptance

00:01:39.630 --> 00:01:41.167
you'll die from their rejection.

00:01:41.167 --> 00:01:42.280
And that's what I would tell people

00:01:42.280 --> 00:01:45.230
because I'd tell myself
'cause I was so worried

00:01:45.230 --> 00:01:46.602
about being accepted.

00:01:46.602 --> 00:01:47.603
These people to accept me.

00:01:47.603 --> 00:01:49.011
These people to accept me.

00:01:49.011 --> 00:01:51.775
And when they don't, you
die, you crumble inside,

00:01:51.775 --> 00:01:54.518
you devastated but if you
already know who you are,

00:01:54.518 --> 00:01:56.575
like I feel like I'm made in God's image,

00:01:56.575 --> 00:01:59.698
my worth and value cannot be tainted.

00:01:59.698 --> 00:02:02.235
You can't add to my work,
you can't take away from it.

00:02:02.235 --> 00:02:03.635
I was born with it.

00:02:03.635 --> 00:02:05.995
And so I don't have to
fight for your approval

00:02:05.995 --> 00:02:06.965
or your acceptance and I want

00:02:06.965 --> 00:02:08.547
my younger self to know that.

00:02:08.547 --> 00:02:10.796
Be confident in who God made me to be

00:02:10.796 --> 00:02:12.714
and be the best me I could be.

00:02:12.714 --> 00:02:15.682
You know, my album, book
probably be correlated,

00:02:15.682 --> 00:02:18.309
it's anomaly because I feel
like I exist as an anomaly.

00:02:18.309 --> 00:02:21.101
Nobody knows what to do
with me a lot of times.

00:02:21.101 --> 00:02:21.934
Know what I'm saying?

00:02:21.934 --> 00:02:24.019
It's like gospel's like wait,
no he's, what is going on?

00:02:24.019 --> 00:02:24.864
I don't get it.

00:02:24.864 --> 00:02:27.684
And hip-hop is like wait, isn't he?

00:02:27.684 --> 00:02:28.842
You know, so nobody really knows like

00:02:28.842 --> 00:02:31.509
what's happening with this dude.

00:02:32.818 --> 00:02:37.377
Yet and still, there's a
lane that I'm running in.

00:02:37.377 --> 00:02:38.210
You know what I mean?

00:02:38.210 --> 00:02:39.384
So it's an anomaly.

00:02:39.384 --> 00:02:41.436
So I'm just kind of like trying
to help people understand

00:02:41.436 --> 00:02:45.251
like how I can run in the
lane that I'm running in

00:02:45.251 --> 00:02:48.394
and still be authentically
me without feeling like

00:02:48.394 --> 00:02:51.061
I have to be this or that.

00:02:51.061 --> 00:02:53.159
But I'm something different all together.

00:02:53.159 --> 00:02:54.500
- [Man] Are you surprised with the amount

00:02:54.500 --> 00:02:56.266
of love that you got?

00:02:56.266 --> 00:02:57.099
- [Man] It's your seventh album.

00:02:57.099 --> 00:02:58.391
It's your seventh album, it's a big step.

00:02:58.391 --> 00:03:00.140
- Number one on iTunes
right now, it's crazy.

00:03:00.140 --> 00:03:01.375
Blowing my mind.

00:03:01.375 --> 00:03:02.792
It blows my mind.

00:03:03.925 --> 00:03:05.375
I don't get it.

00:03:05.375 --> 00:03:06.986
- [Woman] (laughs)

00:03:06.986 --> 00:03:09.026
- I'm being honest, I don't get it.

00:03:09.026 --> 00:03:10.514
I'm just grateful to do music, man.

00:03:10.514 --> 00:03:12.695
Just trying to be authentic,
trying to be myself.

00:03:12.695 --> 00:03:15.240
Be yourself because you know,

00:03:15.240 --> 00:03:16.500
you the best you they'll ever be.

00:03:16.500 --> 00:03:17.727
You're a terrible somebody else.

00:03:17.727 --> 00:03:18.851
- [Man] (laughs)

00:03:18.851 --> 00:03:21.472
- Trying to be somebody,
you're going be found out

00:03:21.472 --> 00:03:23.649
and it's not going to be,
you can't keep that up.

00:03:23.649 --> 00:03:25.529
It's a act and you can't keep that act up.

00:03:25.529 --> 00:03:26.645
It's going to drain you.

00:03:26.645 --> 00:03:28.532
So be yourself because somebody's
always going to be willing

00:03:28.532 --> 00:03:32.834
to invest in something
authentic at some time.

00:03:32.834 --> 00:03:36.145
Not only, man, it was really
like me saying I'm an anomaly.

00:03:36.145 --> 00:03:38.687
I hold a unique space and I'm not trying

00:03:38.687 --> 00:03:40.224
to be anything except myself.

00:03:40.224 --> 00:03:42.619
I think people just...

00:03:42.619 --> 00:03:44.850
I just want people to
embrace being outsiders,

00:03:44.850 --> 00:03:48.215
embrace you are the best
you they'll ever be.

00:03:48.215 --> 00:03:49.357
You're a terrible somebody else.

00:03:49.357 --> 00:03:51.588
So just run in your lane, run your race

00:03:51.588 --> 00:03:53.644
and be who you were made to be.

00:03:53.644 --> 00:03:56.602
So that's kind of the theme of the album.

00:03:56.602 --> 00:03:59.960
It went on to become the
number one album on Billboard

00:03:59.960 --> 00:04:00.842
which was amazing.

00:04:00.842 --> 00:04:02.772
Won a Grammy which was amazing.

00:04:02.772 --> 00:04:05.708
And then I just kind of, you know,

00:04:05.708 --> 00:04:09.328
kept trying to continue to inspire people

00:04:09.328 --> 00:04:11.856
with that type of
mentality of be yourself.

00:04:11.856 --> 00:04:13.466
Your wounds, your scars.

00:04:13.466 --> 00:04:15.891
I got war wounds and I
don't mind sharing 'em

00:04:15.891 --> 00:04:17.648
with people and I talk about it

00:04:17.648 --> 00:04:19.875
and I think people gravitate to that.

00:04:19.875 --> 00:04:20.708
- Let's just talk about the reality

00:04:20.708 --> 00:04:22.192
that even if you're a positive person

00:04:22.192 --> 00:04:23.964
and you're spreading positivity,

00:04:23.964 --> 00:04:25.688
you still go through things,

00:04:25.688 --> 00:04:28.623
you still have temptations,
all of that still happens.

00:04:28.623 --> 00:04:30.777
How do you deal with that as Lecrae.

00:04:30.777 --> 00:04:34.944
- You know, for me, it's
realizing I'm not my failures.

00:04:36.291 --> 00:04:37.124
You know what I mean?

00:04:37.124 --> 00:04:38.508
I think a lot of times
you look at yourself

00:04:38.508 --> 00:04:40.906
and you say man, I messed up, I failed.

00:04:40.906 --> 00:04:43.352
Or you say I am a failure
and that's not true.

00:04:43.352 --> 00:04:44.830
Those are mistakes.

00:04:44.830 --> 00:04:48.812
Like I say in my song, I
count every loss as a lesson.

00:04:48.812 --> 00:04:49.720
You know what I'm saying?

00:04:49.720 --> 00:04:52.363
It's a lesson you learn from
it and you move forward.

00:04:52.363 --> 00:04:55.135
So I don't try to be perfect.

00:04:55.135 --> 00:04:57.800
I don't try to live my life
like I have it all together.

00:04:57.800 --> 00:05:00.294
I try to walk in a direction
of being perfected.

00:05:00.294 --> 00:05:03.685
I try to stay humble, stay
learning, and staying growing,

00:05:03.685 --> 00:05:04.905
and I keep a lot of people around me

00:05:04.905 --> 00:05:06.655
who going to keep me out of the nonsense

00:05:06.655 --> 00:05:09.626
that I probably shouldn't get myself into.

00:05:09.626 --> 00:05:11.350
You are what you eat.

00:05:11.350 --> 00:05:12.699
You are who you hang out with.

00:05:12.699 --> 00:05:13.532
You know what I mean?

00:05:13.532 --> 00:05:14.934
And that's really what's worked for me.

00:05:14.934 --> 00:05:17.805
I think for me, man, I love to...

00:05:17.805 --> 00:05:21.820
Creatively I think I love
to just experience culture.

00:05:21.820 --> 00:05:23.881
I'm like cultural anthropologist, man.

00:05:23.881 --> 00:05:27.907
I just love to just sit and soak up stuff.

00:05:27.907 --> 00:05:31.406
You mess around and see
me with my headphones on

00:05:31.406 --> 00:05:33.402
listening to just merengue all day long

00:05:33.402 --> 00:05:34.440
or something like that.

00:05:34.440 --> 00:05:36.682
A lot of people have checked out my iPod

00:05:36.682 --> 00:05:40.003
and said like why do you have this?

00:05:40.003 --> 00:05:41.966
Like where did you get this from?

00:05:41.966 --> 00:05:42.799
You know what I'm saying?

00:05:42.799 --> 00:05:45.376
I just love to just hear new things

00:05:45.376 --> 00:05:47.064
that are creatively inspire me.

00:05:47.064 --> 00:05:49.484
And then in hip-hop it's tough

00:05:49.484 --> 00:05:51.702
because I feel like it's
just been at a stagnant place

00:05:51.702 --> 00:05:54.338
and I hear a lot of
great truth communicated

00:05:54.338 --> 00:05:56.311
from the Christian hip-hop community.

00:05:56.311 --> 00:05:58.614
But me and Flame were
just talking about it.

00:05:58.614 --> 00:06:01.118
We just like to see artists
stretch themselves creatively

00:06:01.118 --> 00:06:03.976
because I don't think it's as...

00:06:03.976 --> 00:06:07.446
Hip-hop is not as just
this grimy, underground,

00:06:07.446 --> 00:06:08.699
it doesn't have to be polished,

00:06:08.699 --> 00:06:11.087
it doesn't have to be
musical sound anymore.

00:06:11.087 --> 00:06:15.254
It's grown and it's matured
to become a popular platform

00:06:15.254 --> 00:06:17.587
for the whole world to view.

00:06:19.557 --> 00:06:22.140
From Africa to dog-gone Europe.

00:06:23.281 --> 00:06:26.011
And so I think you can't just...

00:06:26.011 --> 00:06:27.366
I think you do have to think through that

00:06:27.366 --> 00:06:28.819
and you do have to be more creative

00:06:28.819 --> 00:06:32.486
and so you know, I just
want to stretch myself

00:06:32.486 --> 00:06:34.645
in that way, in that capacity.

00:06:34.645 --> 00:06:37.365
- We have a lot of listeners
and we have a lot of people

00:06:37.365 --> 00:06:39.622
that want to do their own thing as far

00:06:39.622 --> 00:06:40.623
as their label is concerned.

00:06:40.623 --> 00:06:42.339
What made you decide to go out

00:06:42.339 --> 00:06:44.528
and say this is what I
need to do for myself

00:06:44.528 --> 00:06:47.711
because I know this is what
the world needs to hear?

00:06:47.711 --> 00:06:51.771
- I think it just came down to realizing

00:06:51.771 --> 00:06:53.890
that we have something unique

00:06:53.890 --> 00:06:56.129
and sometimes people don't believe

00:06:56.129 --> 00:06:58.275
in what you're doing and
they don't want to invest

00:06:58.275 --> 00:06:59.123
in what you're doing.

00:06:59.123 --> 00:07:00.470
So you have to invest in yourself

00:07:00.470 --> 00:07:01.873
and you have to believe in yourself

00:07:01.873 --> 00:07:04.373
and create it and push it solo

00:07:05.366 --> 00:07:08.309
and not worry about if someone's
going to come alongside

00:07:08.309 --> 00:07:09.783
or support you.

00:07:09.783 --> 00:07:12.262
Because you know what you
have is real and authentic

00:07:12.262 --> 00:07:14.639
and legit and people resonate with it.

00:07:14.639 --> 00:07:18.012
That inspired me to just keep pushing.

00:07:18.012 --> 00:07:20.245
And everybody that I hired I looked up to,

00:07:20.245 --> 00:07:21.986
like Lucy, like Diddy,
you hear all the stories

00:07:21.986 --> 00:07:23.231
of how nobody believed in 'em

00:07:23.231 --> 00:07:24.625
and they just had to keep working.

00:07:24.625 --> 00:07:26.026
And that's what happened for us

00:07:26.026 --> 00:07:29.827
and we just kept working and believe in

00:07:29.827 --> 00:07:32.461
what we had to offer the world.

00:07:32.461 --> 00:07:34.294
And it was successful.

00:07:35.829 --> 00:07:38.250
- Negativity in hip-hop.

00:07:38.250 --> 00:07:40.331
You see a lot of it,
obviously in social media

00:07:40.331 --> 00:07:42.139
you see a lot of division.

00:07:42.139 --> 00:07:43.971
People going back and forth at each other.

00:07:43.971 --> 00:07:45.867
It always kind of startles me, you know,

00:07:45.867 --> 00:07:47.787
grown men will have
problems with each other.

00:07:47.787 --> 00:07:49.214
That's just going to happen, right?

00:07:49.214 --> 00:07:51.319
But it's kind of like you're in the hood,

00:07:51.319 --> 00:07:52.429
trying to get out of the hood,

00:07:52.429 --> 00:07:53.920
do better for your family, your mother,

00:07:53.920 --> 00:07:55.756
and everybody and then
you finally do better

00:07:55.756 --> 00:07:58.276
but it's almost like you're
going backwards-like.

00:07:58.276 --> 00:08:01.172
You're trying to mess it
up for the whole culture.

00:08:01.172 --> 00:08:02.482
What's some of your thoughts on that?

00:08:02.482 --> 00:08:04.254
When you see people on
social media riffing

00:08:04.254 --> 00:08:06.290
and beefing and going at each other?

00:08:06.290 --> 00:08:08.846
Kind of just putting that
negativity out there?

00:08:08.846 --> 00:08:11.075
- I think, man, you know,
it's part of maturity.

00:08:11.075 --> 00:08:13.522
It's part of us just learning to grow up.

00:08:13.522 --> 00:08:14.849
Stop being crabs in a barrel.

00:08:14.849 --> 00:08:16.004
Learn how to support each other.

00:08:16.004 --> 00:08:19.188
Learn how to just be a real community

00:08:19.188 --> 00:08:20.977
'cause that's how you win is you stand

00:08:20.977 --> 00:08:23.156
on each other's shoulders
and not tear each other

00:08:23.156 --> 00:08:23.989
down all the time.

00:08:23.989 --> 00:08:26.602
And as it pertains to haters
and people just always

00:08:26.602 --> 00:08:28.155
who got something negative to say,

00:08:28.155 --> 00:08:30.535
you know, I just said
this a little while ago,

00:08:30.535 --> 00:08:32.295
I said it's better to create something

00:08:32.295 --> 00:08:34.375
that other people criticize
than to create nothing

00:08:34.375 --> 00:08:36.010
and criticize others.

00:08:36.010 --> 00:08:36.843
You know what I'm saying?

00:08:36.843 --> 00:08:38.225
So it's like somebody always
going to have something to say.

00:08:38.225 --> 00:08:39.361
I mean you doing something right.

00:08:39.361 --> 00:08:40.636
If somebody got something negative to say

00:08:40.636 --> 00:08:42.727
about what you got going on, that's okay.

00:08:42.727 --> 00:08:44.435
Keep doing your thing 'cause they spending

00:08:44.435 --> 00:08:45.832
all their energy talking about

00:08:45.832 --> 00:08:48.293
what you're doing not doing something.

00:08:48.293 --> 00:08:51.057
And so I'm like, man, it's
just going to be the reality

00:08:51.057 --> 00:08:52.958
but just keep your
positive, keep your pushing

00:08:52.958 --> 00:08:54.946
and don't even give them the time of day.

00:08:54.946 --> 00:08:56.950
- When you're looking all
this like Mase, right?

00:08:56.950 --> 00:09:00.522
And Mase was a pastor,
he had a congregation

00:09:00.522 --> 00:09:02.899
and he taught that congregation
and it was positive

00:09:02.899 --> 00:09:05.574
and then he came back
into rapping and the rap

00:09:05.574 --> 00:09:07.993
that he's doing is not
necessarily Christian

00:09:07.993 --> 00:09:08.826
rap.
- Secular.

00:09:08.826 --> 00:09:09.659
- Yeah, it's very secular.

00:09:09.659 --> 00:09:11.147
- [Lecrae] It is very secular, yeah.

00:09:11.147 --> 00:09:13.607
- How do you feel about
things of that nature?

00:09:13.607 --> 00:09:17.190
- I think, man, I'm
about being consistent.

00:09:18.025 --> 00:09:20.792
I'm not an advocate
and that's for anybody.

00:09:20.792 --> 00:09:22.645
It's just Mase or whoever.

00:09:22.645 --> 00:09:25.855
It's about you know, you don't
want to create confusion.

00:09:25.855 --> 00:09:27.142
Like where do you stand?

00:09:27.142 --> 00:09:30.051
Or what side of the fence
are you playing here?

00:09:30.051 --> 00:09:31.209
And just be consistent.

00:09:31.209 --> 00:09:32.740
I think nobody...

00:09:32.740 --> 00:09:33.800
And that's really what I'm trying to do

00:09:33.800 --> 00:09:36.289
in a lot of ways is show
people, like listen man,

00:09:36.289 --> 00:09:39.609
you can still hold on to your faith

00:09:39.609 --> 00:09:43.621
and your core values and
beliefs and make music

00:09:43.621 --> 00:09:48.101
that is not necessarily explicitly
let's walk through Jonah.

00:09:48.101 --> 00:09:48.941
You know what I mean?

00:09:48.941 --> 00:09:49.934
- [Man] (laughs)

00:09:49.934 --> 00:09:54.129
- Without just being like
contrary to what you believe.

00:09:54.129 --> 00:09:55.428
You know what I'm saying?

00:09:55.428 --> 00:09:56.802
It's like for me to make a street record

00:09:56.802 --> 00:09:59.213
doesn't mean I got to start
misogynizing women and

00:09:59.213 --> 00:10:00.123
- [Both] And shoot people.

00:10:00.123 --> 00:10:01.074
- You know what I mean?

00:10:01.074 --> 00:10:02.518
- [Man] You're in an
interesting situation right now

00:10:02.518 --> 00:10:05.217
because for a lot of people
you're still a new artist

00:10:05.217 --> 00:10:06.928
but you've been doing this.

00:10:06.928 --> 00:10:09.700
So how does that kind of like work

00:10:09.700 --> 00:10:12.802
as an introduction to people as you know,

00:10:12.802 --> 00:10:14.771
but still have this big fan base?

00:10:14.771 --> 00:10:17.815
- I don't mind people
seeing me as as new artist.

00:10:17.815 --> 00:10:18.648
You know what I mean?

00:10:18.648 --> 00:10:19.481
'Cause it keep you hungry.

00:10:19.481 --> 00:10:20.511
It keep you on your ground
and keep you humble,

00:10:20.511 --> 00:10:21.893
keep you working hard.

00:10:21.893 --> 00:10:24.193
So I'm not like man, I been here.

00:10:24.193 --> 00:10:25.529
What you talking about?

00:10:25.529 --> 00:10:27.085
You know, I'm like, hey
man, I'm just grateful

00:10:27.085 --> 00:10:28.955
that I got a new fan today.

00:10:28.955 --> 00:10:30.814
You know, it just keeps
it all in perspective

00:10:30.814 --> 00:10:33.585
and plus it's like that's
when people arrive for you.

00:10:33.585 --> 00:10:36.892
When you care about your
fans and you show 'em love

00:10:36.892 --> 00:10:37.725
and you appreciate 'em.

00:10:37.725 --> 00:10:39.716
But when you like, you know...

00:10:39.716 --> 00:10:42.192
I don't understand people be
arguing with fans all day long.

00:10:42.192 --> 00:10:43.363
Get off the internet.

00:10:43.363 --> 00:10:44.946
Go make some music.

00:10:46.378 --> 00:10:48.680
See, some people don't like being broke

00:10:48.680 --> 00:10:52.144
because they feel like something
wrong with being broke.

00:10:52.144 --> 00:10:53.686
But just 'cause you financially broke

00:10:53.686 --> 00:10:55.868
don't mean you're not rich
in other areas of life.

00:10:55.868 --> 00:10:58.701
(crown screaming)

00:11:00.167 --> 00:11:02.204
I been broke before.

00:11:02.204 --> 00:11:04.623
Matter of fact, I grew up
on government assistance.

00:11:04.623 --> 00:11:07.293
You all may not know what
that's like over here but...

00:11:07.293 --> 00:11:10.501
But I been broke and
being broke financially

00:11:10.501 --> 00:11:12.759
made me rich in character.

00:11:12.759 --> 00:11:13.906
Made me rich in loyalty.

00:11:13.906 --> 00:11:15.319
You got to be rich in
loyalty when you broke

00:11:15.319 --> 00:11:18.232
'cause you got to depend on
somebody to take you everywhere.

00:11:18.232 --> 00:11:19.858
Hey, you got my ride bro?

00:11:19.858 --> 00:11:22.275
I got your back for life dog.

00:11:23.243 --> 00:11:26.959
So you know, the best way I could put

00:11:26.959 --> 00:11:29.390
it is like being broke made me rich.

00:11:29.390 --> 00:11:30.507
You feel me?

00:11:30.507 --> 00:11:32.434
I'm rich in areas of life
that I wouldn't be rich in.

00:11:32.434 --> 00:11:34.416
That struggle and that
grind made me something,

00:11:34.416 --> 00:11:35.249
made me who I am.

00:11:35.249 --> 00:11:36.082
(crowd cheering)

00:11:36.082 --> 00:11:38.115
Somebody say being broke made me rich.

00:11:38.115 --> 00:11:39.843
- [Crowd] Being broke made me rich.

00:11:39.843 --> 00:11:41.472
- Come on, say being broke made me rich.

00:11:41.472 --> 00:11:44.389
- [Crowd] Being broke made me rich.

00:11:45.655 --> 00:11:47.394
- Thank you guys so much for watching.

00:11:47.394 --> 00:11:50.520
I made this video because
HardworkDedication asked me to.

00:11:50.520 --> 00:11:52.077
So if there's a famous entrepreneur

00:11:52.077 --> 00:11:53.462
that you want me to profile next,

00:11:53.462 --> 00:11:54.908
check out the link in the description

00:11:54.908 --> 00:11:56.651
and go and cast your vote.

00:11:56.651 --> 00:11:58.722
I also want to give a quick
shout out to Geoff Whaley.

00:11:58.722 --> 00:12:00.923
Geoff, thank you so much for
picking up a copy of my book,

00:12:00.923 --> 00:12:04.230
Your One Word, and posting
that review on your blog.

00:12:04.230 --> 00:12:05.880
I really appreciate the support

00:12:05.880 --> 00:12:07.395
and I'm glad you enjoyed the read.

00:12:07.395 --> 00:12:09.098
So thank you guys again for watching.

00:12:09.098 --> 00:12:10.232
I believe in you.

00:12:10.232 --> 00:12:12.153
I hope you continue to believe in yourself

00:12:12.153 --> 00:12:14.628
and whatever your one word is.

00:12:14.628 --> 00:12:17.371
Much love, I'll see you soon.

00:12:17.371 --> 00:12:20.121
(dramatic music)

00:12:23.535 --> 00:12:24.368
(woman screaming)

00:12:24.368 --> 00:12:26.163
- I have thought about that
time period in my life.

00:12:26.163 --> 00:12:27.650
That was my first music video.

00:12:27.650 --> 00:12:28.923
(woman screaming)

00:12:28.923 --> 00:12:32.168
And I think people like
me you can't throw away.

00:12:32.168 --> 00:12:34.890
But you know who changed a lot.

00:12:34.890 --> 00:12:37.515
You're right, I did change.

00:12:37.515 --> 00:12:39.180
Change is good, you feeling me?

00:12:39.180 --> 00:12:40.474
(crowd cheering)

00:12:40.474 --> 00:12:41.681
Hopefully you've changed.

00:12:41.681 --> 00:12:43.161
(crowd cheering)

00:12:43.161 --> 00:12:45.450
Hopefully you change your
clothes when you get home.

00:12:45.450 --> 00:12:48.847
(crowd laughing)

00:12:48.847 --> 00:12:50.274
There ain't nothing wrong with change.

00:12:50.274 --> 00:12:53.470
Matter of fact, maturity
is not how much you know

00:12:53.470 --> 00:12:56.633
it's how much what you
know has changed you.

00:12:56.633 --> 00:12:59.581
That's what maturity is like.

00:12:59.581 --> 00:13:03.643
But even though I may
change and music may change,

00:13:03.643 --> 00:13:06.391
my style may change, my hair may change,

00:13:06.391 --> 00:13:09.854
my mission ain't never going to change.

00:13:09.854 --> 00:13:12.285
You know I'm more about
creating opportunities.

00:13:12.285 --> 00:13:13.383
We built the studio.

00:13:13.383 --> 00:13:15.097
We got a facility in Atlanta.

00:13:15.097 --> 00:13:15.930
You know what I mean?

00:13:15.930 --> 00:13:16.968
A label.

00:13:16.968 --> 00:13:18.956
We try to hire people.

00:13:18.956 --> 00:13:19.789
You know what I'm saying?

00:13:19.789 --> 00:13:22.156
I'm like trying to create
opportunities and build stuff.

00:13:22.156 --> 00:13:25.266
For me, like I say, I can't
take it with me when I go

00:13:25.266 --> 00:13:27.317
so let me invest, let me create a legacy,

00:13:27.317 --> 00:13:29.985
let me build something that's
bigger than me, beyond me.

00:13:29.985 --> 00:13:32.387
I had a young homey and he was

00:13:32.387 --> 00:13:35.473
in a juvenile detention center,
in the system for a while,

00:13:35.473 --> 00:13:38.114
but his brother was a college student.

00:13:38.114 --> 00:13:41.279
And you know, I asked him, I said,

00:13:41.279 --> 00:13:42.876
the dude who was locked up, I said man,

00:13:42.876 --> 00:13:45.005
why you in the situation you in?

00:13:45.005 --> 00:13:46.538
You know, like the way your life is?

00:13:46.538 --> 00:13:48.136
He said man, 'cause my
daddy was like this.

00:13:48.136 --> 00:13:48.969
This was my dad.

00:13:48.969 --> 00:13:51.947
My dad was always on drugs,
always in and out of prison.

00:13:51.947 --> 00:13:53.161
So then I asked his brother, I said man,

00:13:53.161 --> 00:13:54.757
why are you a college graduate?

00:13:54.757 --> 00:13:56.891
You know you're doing what
you doing and everything else?

00:13:56.891 --> 00:13:59.561
He said 'cause my daddy was
always in and out of jail

00:13:59.561 --> 00:14:01.277
and I wanted to do something different.

00:14:01.277 --> 00:14:03.668
And so man, I just had
to look at my environment

00:14:03.668 --> 00:14:06.659
and my surroundings and say
do I want to repeat the stuff

00:14:06.659 --> 00:14:08.353
that I'm seeing or do I want
to be something different

00:14:08.353 --> 00:14:10.226
than everything that's going on around me?

00:14:10.226 --> 00:14:13.409
And for me, you know, I just
got tired of busting my head.

00:14:13.409 --> 00:14:15.078
Got tired of being in low places

00:14:15.078 --> 00:14:17.481
and making bad decisions and you know,

00:14:17.481 --> 00:14:18.593
police bringing you home.

00:14:18.593 --> 00:14:21.676
It wasn't productive and I'm grateful

00:14:24.036 --> 00:14:26.052
I had good grandmother, good mother

00:14:26.052 --> 00:14:27.242
who just was praying for me

00:14:27.242 --> 00:14:29.755
and just like man,
trying to stay on my head

00:14:29.755 --> 00:14:33.922
and I just had an eye-opening
transformation at like 19.

00:14:34.889 --> 00:14:37.074
And I just got the wheels turning.

00:14:37.074 --> 00:14:38.765
I said I'm not going back.

00:14:38.765 --> 00:14:39.742
You know what I mean?

00:14:39.742 --> 00:14:41.190
Like I'm just going to do
something different with my life

00:14:41.190 --> 00:14:42.940
and that was it man.

